# Birthday Surprise: Setup Guide
 
## 1. Personalize
- script.js: set PARTNER_NAME at the top (replaces every [PARTNER NAME]).
- index.html: replace every [BRACKETED] text: captions, timeline dates/milestones, letter paragraphs, your name, birthday date.
## 2. Add photos and music
Put files in `assets/`:
- photo1.jpg ... photo6.jpg (square-ish, under 500 KB each; add more by copying a `<figure class="polaroid">` block)
- birthday-song.mp3 (exact filename)
Missing photos show a heart placeholder, so the site never looks broken.
## 3. Run in VS Code
1. Open the `birthday-surprise` folder (File > Open Folder).
2. Install the "Live Server" extension.
3. Right-click index.html > "Open with Live Server".
(Or just double-click index.html. Audio works either way.)
## 4. Publish
**Netlify (easiest):** go to app.netlify.com/drop, drag the whole folder in, copy the link.
**GitHub Pages:** create a repo, upload all files (keep `assets/`), then Settings > Pages > Deploy from branch > main / root. Your link appears in a minute.
 
## 5. Testing checklist
- [ ] "Open Your Surprise" scrolls to Memories
- [ ] Photos show (or heart placeholders if missing)
- [ ] "Make a Wish" blows out candles, shows the wish, fires confetti
- [ ] Play starts music; Pause stops it; status text updates
- [ ] Timeline and sections fade in on scroll
- [ ] Letter opens, confetti fires, button changes to Close; closes and reopens
- [ ] "Replay" resets cake, letter, music and scrolls to top
- [ ] Looks right on phone width (use browser dev tools)
- [ ] No errors in the browser console (F12)
- [ ] With OS "reduce motion" on, animations are off and all content is visible
 